    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d176">

                <pb facs="0153" n="147" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg147"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102 Kulangsu/230: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Amoy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacVitty</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Amoy</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-08-09T12:00:00+08:00">August 9,
                        1939—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received August 9—8:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>91. In a conversation yesterday afternoon with Benninghoff,<anchor n="25"
                        xml:id="d176-f1"/> Uchida, the Japanese Consul General, refused to recede
                    from his position as outlined in my 90, August 6, 6 p.m. He offered to recommend
                    the removal of the partial blockade whenever the appointment of a Japanese
                    inspector was agreed to, but would not consider advising the removal of the
                    oppressive measures as a prelude to friendly negotiations. The withdrawal of the
                    landing forces was <pb facs="0154" n="148" xml:id="pg148"/> mentioned only in
                    passing and he had nothing to offer on this subject.</p>
                <p>The conversation was informal and “off the record” and will be repeated in a few
                    days. It seems probable that the Japanese are tired of the whole question and
                    possibly progress may be made in future talks.</p>
                <p>Repeated Chungking, Peiping, Shanghai. Peiping please repeat to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVitty</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d176-f1" n="25" xml:id="d176-f1-content">
                <p>Harry Merrell Benninghoff, Second Secretary of Embassy in China detailed to Amoy
                    as Consul (until September 30).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
